Tata Coffee Limited (formerly known as TCPL Beverages & Foods Limited), is a wholly-owned subsidiary of Tata Consumer Products Limited. As per the Scheme of Arrangement, which took effect on January 1, 2024, the plantation business of the erstwhile Tata Coffee Limited was transferred to and vested in TCPL Beverages & Foods Limited. Subsequently, TCPL Beverages & Foods Limited was renamed as Tata Coffee Limited effective February 2, 2024. Tracing its roots to 1922, Tata Coffee is one of the largest integrated coffee cultivation and processing companies in the world and the largest corporate producer of Indian-origin pepper. Tata Coffee produces around 8000 MT of shade grown Arabica and Robusta coffees, around 800 tons of pepper and around 5500 tons of tea from its 19 coffee estates and 6 tea estates covering 10,000+ ha in Karnataka and Anamallais Hills of Tamil Nadu and Kerala. Additionally, the Company also produces Monsooned Malabar coffee at its facility in Mangalore where the natural monsoon humidity of the region helps create this unique Indian coffee variety with its characteristic earthy flavour.
